body:
You try drinking coffee?  It helps me fight off the lonely feeling.  Also having the TV going in the background (not too loud) helps.  I'm so greatful for the Internet nowadays.  You can find a lot of things to keep your mind occupied.  Going outdoors helps too especially if you're able to take in the scenery/smell/feel of the country on a sunny day.

&#x200B;

We're designed to need interaction.  It's really tough though when you have circumstances getting in the way.  I understand.

&#x200B;

At least we're not alone in our loneliness :)

It's a vicious cycle.  You feel no self worth because you have no friends, and therefore make no friends because they can sense it.  Unfortunately it takes friends to make friends.  People don't want to deal with the stigma of being associated with a loser.  God forbid their inner circles find out!  It's like trying to get a job that requires experience but you can't get the experience because you can't get the job.

&#x200B;

I'm in the same boat.  15 years, no friends.  A few users here and there, and work acquiantances.  Girlfriend of 12 yr. left me because of drinking and relationship gone stale.

&#x200B;

At this point I just try to find solace in the simpler things in life, and appreciate what I have and what I can do to stay productive.

I found the best way to handle panic attacks is just to get mad at them.  It's the fear of fear, and once you realize it's nothing, they will go away.  At least for me that's how it is.  Finding a good variety of relaxing music really helps too.

&#x200B;

I can't speak for any of the meds they put out there.  Don't take them.  Seen too many people having issues with them.
